# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout does.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `ruff format --check` compares bytes, and the CI matrix
# runs on Linux and Windows. A file stored with CRLF would pass the formatting
# gate on one leg of the matrix and fail it on the other, for reasons unrelated
# to the code — and the first Linux run would be the one to discover it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish artefacts that must never be line-ending converted.
*.db binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary

# The lock file is generated. Keep it out of diff review noise, but do keep it
# in the repository: `uv sync --frozen` in CI is meaningless without it.
uv.lock linguist-generated=true -diff
